Package: gdam
Title: Fast robust additive models using gamma divergence
Version: 0.0.1
Date: 2026-09-01
Authors@R: c(
    person("Francis KC", "Hui", , "fhui28@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0765-3533"))
           )
Description: gdam is designed to be a computationally fast (at least at the time of development!) method for robust additive modeling based on the gamma divergence. The package works by assuming an identity link function and a normal distribution for the errors, and then applying the gamma divergence to the resulting restricted maximum likelihood function (REML) to produce a new loss function (hence the name gdam, which stands for gamma divergence additive models) that is design to be most robust to outlying observations. Because gdam takes a `gam` fit from the `mgcv` package as a starting point for optimization of the gamma divergence, and leverages some of the existing methods in the `mgcv` package for estimation and inference, then gadam can exploit many/some of the smoothing options available in the `mgcv` package for additive models.
